      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for a prescription-strength adult dose.\n\n- **Daily maximum:** The ceiling is 3,200 mg/day, usually given as 400\u2013800 mg every 6\u20138 hours. OTC labeling caps it at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1,600 mg is twice the usual 800 mg maximum per dose. Doses above that add little analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit and raise the risk of toxicity.\n- **Risks at this dose:** These include GI bleeding and ulceration, acute kidney injury, fluid retention, hypertension, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove these risks.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common regimen for inflammatory conditions\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** for analgesia\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily\n\nIf you do want 1,600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll note it on the order. I'd still suggest confirming with pharmacy first. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
